[size=6][color=#00ccff][b]AbsoluteHOTAS 4.0.1[/b][/color][/size]
[size=4][b][color=#ffaa00]Native HOTAS, HOSAS, flight-stick, throttle, pedal, and button-box support for Starfield.[/color][/b][/size]

[i]Direct hardware polling and analog ship-control injection. No vJoy, Joystick Gremlin, x360ce, Steam Input, or gamepad emulation. Plug in your hardware, bind it in-game, and fly.[/i][/center]

[line]

[center][size=5][color=#00ff88][b]4.0.1 - stable core release[/b][/color][/size][/center]

4.0.1 is the recommended main file, bringing AbsoluteHOTAS's native analog flight controls and rebuilt in-game configuration workbench to the stable release track.

[b]Profiles and macros are included but remain experimental[/b] while they gain broader real-world hardware and workflow validation. Version 3.0.2 can remain available as a legacy 3.x option; 4.0.1 is the main current download.

[line]

[center][size=5][color=#ffcc00][b]Fly Starfield like a space sim[/b][/color][/size][/center]

[list]
[*][b][color=#00ff88]True Analog Flight Control:[/color][/b] Direct authority over pitch, yaw, roll, strafe, throttle, and reverse without converting flight hardware into a virtual Xbox controller.[/*]
[*][b][color=#00ff88]Flight Axes Workbench:[/color][/b] Bind, invert, tune, calibrate, and monitor every core analog control from one opening page.[/*]
[*][b][color=#00ff88]Hot-Swappable Profiles (Experimental):[/color][/b] Switch bindings, axes, tuning, aim behavior, and macros from a button or maintained selector position.[/*]
[*][b][color=#00ff88]Macro Builder (Experimental):[/color][/b] Create chords, taps, timed holds, ordered sequences, and turbo actions. Named ship actions follow your current Starfield keybinds.[/*]
[*][b]Multi-Device Input:[/b] Mix sticks, throttles, pedals, button boxes, and custom DirectInput hardware in one setup.[/*]
[*][b]Advanced Throttle Support:[/b] Positional or self-centering throttle, reverse zones, detents, cruise controls, boost zones, and pilot turn assist.[/*]
[*][b]Independent Aim and HOSAM/HOSAS Modes:[/b] Separate steering from the weapon reticle, use aim-driven steering, or combine a left-hand stick with native mouse steering.[/*]
[*][b]Respects In-Game Rebinds:[/b] Ship buttons and macro actions reconcile against Starfield's current ControlMap instead of assuming vanilla keys.[/*]
[/list]

[line]

[center][size=5][color=#00ccff][b]What changed in 4.0.1[/b][/color][/size][/center]

[list]
[*]Promoted the validated flight-control and configuration core to stable.[/*]
[*]Redesigned the opening Flight Axes page so binding, tuning, calibration, and live input feedback are all in one place.[/*]
[*]Improved compatibility and stability around overlays, frame-generation tools, graphics injectors, and translation layers.[/*]
[*]Strengthened configuration validation, diagnostics, cleanup, and automated regression coverage.[/*]
[/list]

[b]Compatibility note:[/b] If a graphics utility conflicts with the workbench, configure and save AbsoluteHOTAS with that utility disabled, then set [b][UI] bEnableWorkbench = false[/b] before re-enabling it. Flight controls and saved configurations continue to work. See the changelog and full guide for technical details.

[line]

[center][size=5][color=#ff5555][b]Important 4.0 Upgrade Notice[/b][/color][/size][/center]

[b]Updating from 4.0.0-beta:[/b] replace the DLL and shipped AbsoluteHOTAS.ini. Keep AbsoluteHOTAS_Custom.ini and Profiles; they are user-owned and are not included in the archive.

[b]Updating from 3.x:[/b] 4.0 is a fresh configuration baseline. Do not copy a 3.x AbsoluteHOTAS.ini into this release or import it as a 4.0 profile. Back up the old file for reference, install both new files, and rebuild through the workbench.

[line]

[center][size=5][color=#00ccff][b]Install and fly[/b][/color][/size][/center]

[b]Requirements[/b]
[list]
[*]Starfield 1.16.242 or 1.16.244[/*]
[*]SFSE 0.2.20 or later[/*]
[*]No Starfield Address Library required[/*]
[/list]

[list=1]
[*]Install the archive normally with your mod manager.[/*]
[*]Launch Starfield through SFSE.[/*]
[*]Open the Starfield main or pause menu and press [color=#ffaa00][b]Ctrl+Alt+B[/b][/color].[/*]
[*]Bind your primary flight axes and desired ship buttons.[/*]
[*]Choose a convenient controller button for future workbench access, then click [b]Save & Close[/b].[/*]
[/list]

[i]For full mouse interaction, open the workbench from a Starfield menu. During gameplay the game retains its mouse lock; standard keyboard navigation remains available.[/i]

